For Google DeepMind L6 / Senior Staff-level system-design preparation with 9+ years of Java backend experience, 
I would not start with “design Amazon” as one giant system.

For interview preparation, the better approach is to use an e-commerce system as a progressive system-design case study, 
where each stage introduces a deeper distributed-systems problem.

My recommendation:
      Use Amazon-like e-commerce as the primary system, but define the scope as:

              Design a large-scale e-commerce platform —>
                              Amazon/Flipkart-style —>
                                      supporting product discovery, 
                                      inventory, 
                                      cart, 
                                      order placement, 
                                      payment, and order fulfillment.


This is better than designing only eBay because it exposes more of the distributed-system problems that are valuable at L6.
