4. Identify the critical business flow

The most important flow is:

                  Search
                     ↓
                  Product
                     ↓
                  Cart
                     ↓
                  Checkout
                     ↓
                  Inventory
                     ↓
                  Payment
                     ↓
                  Order


But notice something important.
            The order of these operations isn't necessarily the same as the logical dependency.

For example:
            Customer clicks "Buy"
                    ↓
            Can I actually sell this product?
                    ↓
            Is inventory available?
                    ↓
            Can I reserve it?
                    ↓
            Can I collect payment?
                    ↓
            Can I create/confirm the order?

This is going to become extremely important later.
