10. Identify critical vs non-critical operations

            This is another L6-level distinction.
            
            Consider:            
                        Product description:                        
                              If it takes:  200 ms
                        
                        instead of: 50 ms
            
            it's undesirable, but usually not a catastrophic business failure.

      Now consider:      
                  Inventory reservation:                  
                  If two users purchase the last item:                  
                                                      Stock = 1                  
                                                      User A → reserve
                                                      User B → reserve
      
                  and both succeed:
      
      Stock becomes inconsistent
      
      That's much more serious.

Therefore:
            | Operation           | Requirement                                 |
            | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
            | Product description | High availability + low latency             |
            | Search              | High availability + low latency             |
            | Cart                | High availability                           |
            | Inventory           | Stronger correctness                        |
            | Order               | Strong consistency around state transitions |
            | Payment             | Very high correctness                       |
            | Analytics           | Can usually be asynchronous                 |

This is going to drive our architecture.
